ality of the balanced meal plate model#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/I92K9RF4","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 19","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=19&annotation=5I48ENHC","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=3&annotation=F6VGFW76","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 12","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=12&annotation=9FZ543AG","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=3&annotation=PCBAV7LI","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 15","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=15&annotation=ECR3DBSY","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 15","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=15&annotation=LG578LRM","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=3&annotation=PXU496IB","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 15","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/IYTC2J8B?page=15&annotation=QDRZ4Z3J","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model","Authors":"Worasit Choochaiwattana, Patinya Jaruariyanon, Assaree Jitpranee, Rawirin Deecharoen, Thanaporn Kaewpradup, Charoonsri Chusak, Sirichai Adisakwattana","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1038/s41598-025-29631-w","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"The 2:1:1 dietary proportion model, promoting balanced eating, 20 faces challenges in practical application due to difficulty in visually 21 estimating portion sizes. To address this, we developed an artificial 22 intelligence (AI)-based application to assist in the accurate assessment of 23 2:1:1 dietary proportion. This study demonstrated the accuracy of the AI 24 application compared to estimates made by nutrition and dietetics 25 students (ND) and registered dietitians (RD), while also assessing user 26 satisfaction and attitudes. The AI application was trained using images of 27 three popular Thai dishes: Hainanese Chicken Rice, Shrimp Paste Fried 28 Rice, and Egg Noodle, each prepared in three portion variationThese weight-based proportions were established as the reference 387 standard for training and evaluating the AI model. Although the AI model 388 estimates visual area proportions based on image analysis, the reference 389 standard for model validation was derived from the exact weight 390 measurements to ensure data integrity. Additionally, pixel-wise 391 annotations were performed to visually segment each food component 392 within the images, representing relative area proportion","Findings":"The AI 29 system demonstrated significantly lower mean absolute error (MAE) than 30 both ND and RD groups in estimating proportions for Hainanese Chicken 31 Rice and Shrimp Paste Fried Rice (p < 0.05), indicating superior accuracy.  32 User satisfaction surveys revealed that 61% of participants rated their 33 overall experience with the application as moderate, with suggestions for 34 improving accuracy. Over half agreed that the AI tool shows potential as a 35 practical resource for nutrition education and dietary assessmentThe AI-Based application demonstrated superior accuracy in 223 estimating dietary proportions compared to human estimators, 224 particularly for complex Asian dishes like Hainanese Chicken Rice and 225 Shrimp Paste Fried Rice","Conclusions":"The AI 36 holds promise as a tool for promoting adherence to the 2:1:1 model and 37 facilitating healthy lifestyle changesMoreover, the application offers significant value for nutrition and 293 dietetics students by providing a platform to practice portion estimation 294 and develop key dietetic skills, such as dietary counseling and behavior 295 management, in preparation for their careersFor registered dietitians, the tool provides an opportunity to reskill 302 and refine their portion estimation abilities. It serves as a valuable 303 resource for demonstrating appropriate portion sizes and balanced meals 304 to patients in a simple, visually engaging way. Integrating the tool into 305 clinical practice can enhance patient education, helping individuals better 306 understand portion control and the 2:1:1 dietary model. This combination 307 of improving patient understanding and refining professional skills makes 308 the AI-powered application a versatile tool for promoting healthy eating 309 and supporting improved dietary outcomes.","Limitations":"First, the AI model was trained on a limited dataset of three Thai dishes, 312 which may limit the generalizability of the results to other foods","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1l0ekp0","at":1769791474154}},"smart_blocks:AI powered dietary proportion assessment for improving accuracy and practicality of the balanced meal plate model.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06506208,-0.0072541,0.02173289,-0.01090975,0.01956918,0.05121616,-0.01639832,0.02859236,0.00947117,-0.00991637,0.01890201,-0.13371268,0.01892145,0.06668768,0.00806372,-0.03456021,0.03157186,-0.00373555,-0.00094566,-0.00487104,0.04534945,-0.04886814,0.01081874,-0.00894592,0.01906101,0.05388525,-0.02523737,-0